Advanced Migration Scenarios
Scenario 1: Batch Migration for Maintenance
When performing node maintenance, you might need to migrate multiple VMs.

Create a batch migration script:
cat << 'EOF' > batch-migrate.sh
#!/bin/bash

SOURCE_NODE=${1}
TARGET_NODE=${2}

if [ -z "$SOURCE_NODE" ] || [ -z "$TARGET_NODE" ]; then
    echo "Usage: $0 <source-node> <target-node>"
    exit 1
fi

echo "Migrating all VMs from $SOURCE_NODE to $TARGET_NODE"

# Get all VMIs running on the source node
VMIS=$(oc get vmi -A -o jsonpath='{range .items[?(@.status.nodeName=="'$SOURCE_NODE'")]}{.metadata.namespace}{" "}{.metadata.name}{"\n"}{end}')

if [ -z "$VMIS" ]; then
    echo "No VMs found on node $SOURCE_NODE"
    exit 0
fi

echo "Found VMs to migrate:"
echo "$VMIS"
echo ""

# Migrate each VM
echo "$VMIS" | while read namespace vm_name; do
    if [ -n "$vm_name" ]; then
        echo "Migrating $vm_name in namespace $namespace..."
        cat << MIGRATION_EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: kubevirt.io/v1
kind: VirtualMachineInstanceMigration
metadata:
  name: ${vm_name}-maintenance-migration
  namespace: $namespace
spec:
  vmiName: $vm_name
  nodeSelector:
    kubernetes.io/hostname: $TARGET_NODE
MIGRATION_EOF
        echo "Migration initiated for $vm_name"
        sleep 2
    fi
done

echo ""
echo "All migrations initiated. Monitor with: oc get vmim -A"
EOF

chmod +x batch-migrate.sh
Use the batch migration script:
# List nodes first
oc get nodes

# Run batch migration (replace with actual node names)
# ./batch-migrate.sh <source-node> <target-node>
Scenario 2: Migration with Constraints
Sometimes you need to migrate VMs with specific constraints or policies.

Create a VM with anti-affinity rules:
cat << EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: kubevirt.io/v1
kind: VirtualMachine
metadata:
  name: constrained-vm
  namespace: default
spec:
  running: true
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        kubevirt.io/vm: constrained-vm
        app: database
    spec:
      affinity:
        podAntiAffinity:
          requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:
          - labelSelector:
              matchExpressions:
              - key: app
                operator: In
                values:
                - database
            topologyKey: kubernetes.io/hostname
      domain:
        devices:
          disks:
          - disk:
              bus: virtio
            name: containerdisk
        resources:
          requests:
            memory: 512Mi
            cpu: 500m
      volumes:
      - containerDisk:
          image: quay.io/kubevirt/cirros-container-disk-demo
        name: containerdisk
EOF
Attempt migration and observe constraint behavior:
virtctl migrate constrained-vm
oc get vmim -w
Troubleshooting Common Migration Issues
Issue 1: Migration Stuck or Failed
Check migration status and conditions:
oc describe vmim <migration-name>
Look for common failure reasons:
oc get events --field-selector reason=FailedMigration -A
Check node resources:
oc describe nodes | grep -E "Name:|Conditions:|Allocated resources:"
Issue 2: VM Not Responding After Migration
Check VM status:
oc get vmi <vm-name> -o yaml | grep -A 20 status:
Restart VM if necessary:
virtctl restart <vm-name>
Check pod logs:
oc logs -l kubevirt.io/vm=<vm-name> --tail=100
Issue 3: Storage-Related Migration Problems
Verify storage class supports migration:
oc get storageclass -o yaml | grep -A 5 -B 5 volumeBindingMode
Check PVC access modes:
oc get pvc -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,ACCESS:.spec.accessModes
